Emerging Market Opportunities
Battery Recycling and Circular Supply Chains
Advanced recycling technologies offer opportunities to recover valuable materials from used battery systems and reduce dependence on newly mined resources. Improved recovery processes and circular supply chain models could support long-term cost management and strengthen the sustainability profile of electric aviation.

Regional Aircraft and Urban Air Mobility
The development of eVTOL aircraft, air taxis, and hybrid-electric regional planes is creating demand for purpose-built aviation battery systems. Regional aircraft may provide an early opportunity for electrification on selected routes, while urban air mobility projects are encouraging collaboration between battery manufacturers and aircraft developers. Battery leasing and energy-as-a-service models could also help operators manage upfront costs.

